Modified files
--------------
The following files carry modifications and/or ports of upstream research
code. Each file states its origin in its module docstring:

  models/minimind.py            MiniMind backbone (model definition unchanged
                                in structure, cleaned for this repository)
  models/vision.py              SigLIP2 wrapper, projector and the V14 action
                                model loader
  agent/vision_tiles.py         5-tile split + TileCompressor + tile_pos
  agent/dsl.py, agent/copy_resolve.py   GUI action DSL (V14 protocol)
  agent/environment.py, agent/ctx_pack.py   MiniWoB++ loop and history packing
  legacy/action_v1.py           the retired V1 JSON action prototype (kept for
                                traceability only)
  scripts/gui_v9_*              V9 grounding ablation ports
  models/grounding.py           GroundingHead, focal loss, offset regression
  scripts/lib/rl.py, scripts/train_grpo.py   V12/V13 GRPO ports
  scripts/filter_teacher.py, scripts/collect_oracle.py,
  scripts/build_distill_dataset.py, scripts/prepare_gui_sft_data.py
                                V10/V11/V14 teacher-distillation data pipeline

Third-party components
----------------------
* SigLIP2 vision encoder (google/siglip2-base-p32-256-ve): external,
  pre-trained weights, Apache License 2.0. The encoder is frozen and is NOT
  part of the from-scratch training claim; its weights are not redistributed
  here.
* BrowserGym and MiniWoB++ (ServiceNow / Farama Foundation): Apache License
  2.0. Used as an evaluation environment only; not vendored.
* OpenApps desktop benchmark environment: Creative Commons
  Attribution-NonCommercial 4.0 International (CC BY-NC 4.0). Used externally
  on HPC for closed-loop evaluation and expert/DAgger data collection; neither
  OpenApps source code nor OpenApps screenshots/trajectories are vendored or
  redistributed here, and any OpenApps-derived V15–V18 checkpoints are
  restricted to non-commercial research use under OpenApps's CC BY-NC 4.0
  terms.
* The V9 grounding head follows the CenterNet (Zhou et al., MIT License)
  centre-point / offset-regression idea. No CenterNet source code is copied;
  only the published formulation is re-implemented.
* PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), Transformers, safetensors, NumPy, PyYAML, Pillow and
  filelock keep their own licenses; they are dependencies, not part of this
  project's license grant.

Data and checkpoints
--------------------
MiniWoB++ screenshots, OpenApps screenshots/trajectories, teacher trajectories
(GUI-Owl / V11 teacher), the V14–V18 distilled datasets and all model
checkpoints are NOT redistributed in this repository. data/README.md documents
the schemas, generation commands and statistics so the datasets can be
regenerated by users who obtain the upstream assets under their own terms.
